<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 13 November, from 1002 to 2015.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/aethelred-the-unready" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aethelred-the-unready.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1002">1002 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,024 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Æthelred II orders the St Brice's Day massacre of Danes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelred-the-unready">Æthelred the Unready</a> ordered the killing of Danish men in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. Victims reputedly included the sister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweyn-forkbeard">Sweyn Forkbeard</a>, who launched repeated invasions and took the English crown in 1013.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1093">1093 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">933 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Malcolm III of Scotland is killed at Alnwick</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Malcolm III was killed in an ambush while besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alnwick">Alnwick</a> Castle in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northumberland">Northumberland</a>, together with his eldest son. A succession struggle followed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1160">1160 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">866 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Louis VII of France marries Adela of Champagne</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-vii-of-france">Louis VII of France</a> married Adela of Champagne, his third wife, who became queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Her son Philip II went on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>, during which Adela was regent of France from 1190 to 1191.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-vii-of-france">Louis VII of France</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1642">1642 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">384 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Parliament's army blocks the Royalists at Turnham Green</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Turnham Green, the much larger Parliamentarian army of the Earl of Essex faced the forces of King Charles I in a standoff. By blocking the Royalist army's way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, Parliament forced Charles to retreat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-english-civil-war">First English Civil War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1715">1715 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">311 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Government forces halt the Jacobite advance at Sheriffmuir</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A smaller government army under the Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argyll">Argyll</a> fought the Jacobite army of the Earl of Mar near Dunblane in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>. Neither side won clearly, but Mar withdrew and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobite-rising-of-1715">Jacobite rising of 1715</a> lost its momentum.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sheriffmuir">Battle of Sheriffmuir</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobite-rising-of-1715">Jacobite rising of 1715</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Kingdom of Great Britain</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1775">1775 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">American forces occupy Montreal</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Continental troops under Richard Montgomery entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a> unopposed during the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>. The campaign collapsed after the failed assault on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> City at the end of the year.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Charles withdraws from Hungarian affairs</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Eckartsau, Charles I renounced any part in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>'s government, two days after a similar declaration for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> was effectively at an end.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2015">2015 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">11 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Coordinated terrorist attacks kill 130 in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Islamic State gunmen and suicide bombers attacked the Bataclan concert hall, cafés and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stade">Stade</a> de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. It was the deadliest attack in France since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, and a state of emergency followed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li></ol>
